Who was it that said that I manage to do make all kinds of stupid
mistakes and survive them?  Here's the counterpoint.

I played carefully with my knight.  Poision resistance was hard to get,
so I didn't drop below minetown.  I made a return trip or two and had
all nine easy protection points.

I had at least three unicorn horns by the time I finally picked up
poison resistance, then found a new bottom level in the mines that I'd
never seen before.

Along the way, I'd foolishly diluted three black potions after finding
one with a nymph and presuming it was the usual.  Turns out I'd killed
her fast; it was full healing.

Nonetheless, I was happily roaming the dungeon, and found that Sir_Hawk
makes a much better knight god than Lugh.  He gave me greyswandir rather
quickly, though he followed it shortly thereafter with werebane.

I went through several mounts; a couple underneath me and several that
died fighting on their own.

Two wraiths and a succubus brought me to level 14 for the quest.

Off I went, though my mount was killed before I got to Arthur.
Continuing was my fatal mistake.

I tried to take on Ixoth on foot with greyswandir.  She summoned, I used
a cursed teleport scroll.  She followed, but left the friends she'd
summoned behind.  A little maneuvering gtot me to a safe level, where I
healed and went back again.

I prayed--but wasn't low enough in HP, and got crowned instead. (Huh?
Does that mean that the laptop still has 3.4.0 on it?  I thought
crowning now only happened on altars).

I escaped and healed again, and returned.

Dumb, dumb, dumb.  I should have been twoweaponing lances, not fighting
on foot.  It was actually an elvenking (? it was blue) that got me.

*sigh*

